    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/continual-progress.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "Bean edits are pushed to the state branch, not the PR",
      "prov:value": "Under the state branch architecture (proposal `cat-harness/docs/proposals/state-branch-2026-10-02.md`),\nbean edits (`beans/defs/*.md`, `beans/workflows/*.json`) do not belong in the\nPR's commit set.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "docs/proposals/state-branch-2026-10-02.md",
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/continual-progress.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The fifth invariant, and the one agents get wrong",
      "prov:value": "Measured, 2026-09-16. A documentation change with five generated diagrams was\ngreen, unreviewed and unmerged, held back with three SVGs attached in chat and a\nnote that the layout was machine-accepted but not confirmed legible. The\nauthor's reply was *\"jsut merge so i can help assess\"*. The hold made assessment\nharder, not safer, and cost a round-trip to someone who types with difficulty.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-16"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/continual-progress.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Link the PAGE, never the site root",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-21, after a session that had pointed three times at\n`…/branches/<branch>/` while asking about the navbar on the IRIS replica:\n\n> *\"next time give appropraite link\n> https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/claude-determined-euler-gqhkk0/who-iris/\"*\n\nThe root is not a shortcut, it is a handoff of the last step. It makes the\nreader reconstruct a route the agent already knew, and it does it to the person\nthis repository's interaction profile exists for — one who types with\ndifficulty. Every extra click is a cost the agent chose not to pay and passed\non.\n\nIt also hides a real failure mode. An agent that links the root has not checked\nthat its page is reachable at all: `/<iris-replica>/` 404ed for an hour in that same\nsession, under a root that loaded perfectly.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/continual-progress.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A pipe discards the exit code — so a piped run cannot verify anything",
      "prov:value": "This is mechanical rather than a matter of care, and it is written down because\ncare did not prevent it. Twice in one session, 2026-09-20:\n\n- `gen-site-jsonld --check` on a genuinely stale tree. `… | tail -8; echo $?`\n  printed **0**. Caught within the minute — and the commit message that fixed\n  it said \"worth checking rather than assuming\".\n- `site:links` from the repository root, two hours later. Read the message,\n  never checked `$?`, and **opened a bean** asserting a defect that does not\n  exist: the script exits 2 and always has. Scrapped as `ipth`.\n\nThe second is the expensive shape. A command whose output *sounds* like a\nfailure, run through a pipe, reads as a silent pass — and a silent pass is\nprecisely what this repository treats as worse than a loud failure. The first\ncost a minute; the second cost a bean, a wrong diagnosis, and very nearly a\n\"fix\" to working code.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ipth",
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/continual-progress.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "A template is not a page — verify the BUILD, not the source of it",
      "prov:value": "Measured, 2026-09-20, and it is worth the detail because every safeguard fired\ngreen. `docs/_includes/landing.html` builds a sticky's `<article>` opening tag\nacross many lines. One Liquid `{% endif -%}` right-stripped the newline before\nthe next attribute, so the tag emitted as\n\n```\n…--fa-text-scale:0.74;\"aria-labelledby=\"fa-sticky-cat-harness-summary\"\n```\n\nTwo attributes with no separator is an unparseable tag. `index.md` is\n**markdown**, so Kramdown stopped recognising the block as HTML and escaped all\nof it. The published landing page — the live site and every staging preview —\ncarried `&lt;article class=\"fa-sticky …\"` as **visible words**, with\n`&lt;/article&gt;` to match: 3 escaped, 0 real. Every `.fa-landing-sticky--fixed`\nrule was dead, which was the whole feature.\n\nWhat passed over it: 3517 unit tests, `eslint`, `tsc`, twelve gates, the e2e\nsuite **and** the accessibility suite. Not one of them was wrong. Every one reads\na **source**, and the source was valid HTML — the defect exists only in the\noutput of the markdown converter. The agent had rendered and screenshotted the\ntemplate through a scratch harness and called the round verified.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/continual-progress.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "A template is not a page — verify the BUILD, not the source of it",
      "prov:value": "The general form of the gap now has a check — `check:escaped-markup`, run in\n`docs-site.yml` against the assembled `_site/`, because that is the only place\nthe answer exists. But a check written after the fact does not retire the rule:\nthe next defect of this shape will be in whatever the build does that no source\ngate can see."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/continual-progress.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Green means handed to the Merge Steward — an agent never merges to `main` here",
      "prov:value": "**The owner's merge policy for folio-assistant, 2026-10-01 (arc `3fva`).** It\nis the \"explicit merge permission\" case above, made into a hand-off rather\nthan a question:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 3fva",
        "2026-10-01"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/continual-progress.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Pace the ready marking — the runner pool is shared",
      "prov:value": "**The owner's ruling, 2026-10-24 (\"C. Pace agents\").** The Actions runner pool\nis shared across the owner's repositories. A draft PR runs only the fast tier,\nand marking it ready starts the full tier, about 10 jobs (bean `dft1`). So the\nnumber of PRs marked ready at once is what fills the queue:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean dft1",
        "2026-10-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/continual-progress.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Pace the ready marking — the runner pool is shared",
      "prov:value": "the fast\ntier is green, and the hand-off above waits for the full tier. Measured on\n2026-10-24: 28 queued PR runs against 5 runners, from 28 different PRs opened\nwithin an hour, mostly agent branches. A fix PR waited hours behind them.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/continual-progress.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Two green PRs can merge into a red main, and the answer is to fix forward",
      "prov:value": "branch contained. On 2026-09-24 that happened: #1245 added a generated\nreport, and main had just gained a workflow instance the report did not\ncover. Main went red at #1245's merge, and no `regen` on either branch could\nhave seen it (bean `391j`).\n\n**The owner's policy is to fix forward, not to add a merge queue or an\n\"up to date\" requirement** (2026-09-24). So:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 391j",
        "#1245",
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/continual-progress.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Two green PRs can merge into a red main, and the answer is to fix forward",
      "prov:value": "- **Watch main's CI after every merge of yours**, not only your PR's —\n  whoever pressed the button.\n  \"My PR was green\" does not mean main is green.\n- **A red main whose failure your diff did not cause is still yours to fix\n  when you find it.** Establish the cause from the failing run and each\n  parent's history first, then regenerate or repair in a small PR of its own,\n  and merge it as soon as it is green. #1249 and #1257 each did this within\n  minutes.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1249",
        "#1257"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/continual-progress.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Two green PRs can merge into a red main, and the answer is to fix forward",
      "prov:value": "#1249 and #1257 each did this within\n  minutes.\n- **Do not blame the last merge because it is the last merge.** Check whether\n  the parent was already red. In `391j` it was, and the first diagnosis (\"a\n  blind spot in `regen`\") was wrong for exactly that reason.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 391j",
        "#1249",
        "#1257"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
